

Variables
------------------
Name of storage location is called variable

In java 3 types of variable support

1.local variable
-------------------
Any variable declare inside method/block is called local variable

scope: Within a method/block
Memory allocation: at the time of method execution
Memory deallocate: after method execution

2.Instance variable
------------------------
Any variable declared inside the class and outside the any method/block
then such variable called instance

scope: Within Object
Memory allocation: Once Object created 
Memory deallocate: After object release

3.Static variable
---------------------
Any variable declared using static keyword inside the class and outside the any method/block
then such variable called static variable

static keyword plays important in Java used for memory management
Scope: Within a class
Memory allocate: as soon as class loaded
Memory deallocate: after class unload

Note:
-------------
Static data always get only one time memory and same memory it can be shared
with multiple objects

-common data for all object you can declared with static

--------------------------------------------------
Methods Types
---------------
1.Instance method
------------------------------
Instance method is method which declared without static keyword and this
method we always call only through object

2.static method
---------------------
Static method we declared using static keyword
1.Static method we can call directly through its classname(no Object required)
2.If you are calling static method in same class then without class name also we can call


Automation reusable method (static method)


==========================================================
Static Keyword
===============
static keyword help for memory management
static keyword we can apply for variable and method

Static Block
==================
Any code wrriten in static block will always get first priority
Static block is used to initialize static variable


this Keyword, super keyword & final keyword
	we can use in inheritance

this keyword is used to refer current class variable,method and constructor.

Super Keyword
============================
1.Super keyword can be used to refer immediate parent class instance variable.
2.Super keyword can be used to invoke immediate parent class method.
3.Super keyword can be used to call immediate parent class constructor.(super())

final Keyword
======================================
final keyword can be apply for variable,method and class
1.If we apply final keyword to variable then that variable will be consider constant variable
(value will become fix...no one can update)
2.If we apply final keyword to method then we cant override that method in other class or child class
3.If we apply final keyword to class then we can not extend that class into another class.
===============================================================
IQ: How we can implement immutable class ,variable or method in java?
Ans: Using final keyword.
==============================================================







Data Abstraction
================
It is process of hiding implementation details of software from end user, and providing
relevant features to the user

Abstraction achive using
------------------------------
1.Abstarct class
2.Interface

1.Abstarct class
===============
1.In abstract class we can have both abstract method and non abstarct (concreate) Methods.
2.Abstract method and class we can declare using abstract keyword.
3.Abstract class can not be instantiated.
4.Abstract methods must be overriden by class which inherits abstract class.
5.Using Abstract class partial abstraction is possible.

Interface
===========
1.An interface in java is a blueprint of a class. 
2.Interface contains final and static variables.
3.Interface contains abstract methods.
4.An abstract method is a method contains definition but not body.
5.Methods in interface are public by default.
6.Interface supports the functionality of multiple inheritance.
7.We can define interface with interface keyword.
8.A class extends another class, an interface extends another interface
 but a class implements an interface.
9.We can create Object reference for Interface but we cannot instantiate interface.
10.Inheritance use extends keyword and Interface use implements keyword.





















